Playwright is a browser automation tool that allows your program to control a web browser automatically.
--> So instead of a human controlling the browser, your program controls it.
--> Playwright communicates with the browser and tells it what to do.
Playwright
    │
    ├── Launch browser
    │
    ├── Open page
    │
    ├── Navigate to website
    │
    ├── Find button
    │
    ├── Click button
    │
    └── Verify result
--> Playwright is the tool controlling the browser.

Playwright does not automatically click buttons, Playwright can perform two major types of work:
A. Actions : Tell the website to do something.
--> Click
--> Type
--> Select
--> Hover
--> Upload
--> Scroll
--> Press keyboard key
B. Verification : Check what happened.
--> Is the dashboard visible?
--> Did the URL change?
--> Is the Login button still visible?
--> Does the page contain "Welcome"?
--> Is the button disabled?
┌──────────────────┐
│   Your Program   │
└────────┬─────────┘
         ↓
┌──────────────────┐
│    Playwright    │
└────────┬─────────┘
         ↓
┌──────────────────┐
│     Browser      │
└────────┬─────────┘
         ↓
┌──────────────────┐
│     Website      │
└──────────────────┘

Browser automation --> A program controls a browser.
Browser testing --> A program controls a browser and verifies that the application behaves correctly.

Browser Context : A separate, isolated browsing environment/session inside the browser.
Browser
   │
   ├── Browser Context 1
   │       │
   │       ├── Page 1
   │       └── Page 2
   │
   └── Browser Context 2
           │
           └── Page 1
--> One Browser can have multiple Contexts
┌──────────────────────┐
│       Browser        │
│                      │
│  ┌────────────────┐  │
│  │ Browser Context│  │
│  │                │  │
│  │ ┌────────────┐ │  │
│  │ │   Page     │ │  │
│  │ │            │ │  │
│  │ │  Website   │ │  │
│  │ │     ↓      │ │  │
│  │ │  Locator   │ │  │
│  │ │     ↓      │ │  │
│  │ │   Action   │ │  │
│  │ └────────────┘ │  │
│  └────────────────┘  │
└──────────────────────┘
Browser           → starts the browser.
Browser Context   → manages an isolated login/session environment.
Page              → represents the website/tab.
Locator           → finds the username field, password field, login button, etc.
Action            → fills the username, fills the password, clicks Login.
Assertion         → verifies that login succeeded.

Playwright API :
Playwright API is the collection of commands and functions that Playwright provides so that your program can control a browser.
--> Playwright gives your program commands such as:
1. Launch browser
2. Create context
3. Create page
4. Open URL
5. Click
6. Fill
7. Press
8. Screenshot
9. Check

Playwright architecture :
                    YOUR CODE
                       ↓
                PLAYWRIGHT API
                       ↓
                   PLAYWRIGHT
                       ↓
          ┌────────────┼────────────┐
          ↓            ↓            ↓
      Chromium      Firefox       WebKit
          ↓
    Browser Context
          ↓
         Page
          ↓
       Locator
          ↓
        Action
          ↓
       Website
          ↓
       Result
          ↓
      Assertion

